// Moderator and administrative actions.
//
// Two properties shape this whole file.
//
// The first is that an action must land now. A kick that takes effect when the
// target's token next expires is not a kick; it is a delay with a security hole
// in it. So every verb here writes control-plane state *and* pushes a directive
// to the relays holding the affected sessions, and the response is not returned
// until that push is accepted.
//
// The second is that an action must be attributable. Every call returns the
// `ModerationEntry` it produced, which is the same record the log serves and the
// same record an appeal is heard against. A backend that discards the response
// still cannot escape the entry.

